{"title":"Incenter","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Incenter&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Incenter.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/Incenter.PNG/300px-Incenter.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"173\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/Incenter.PNG/450px-Incenter.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/Incenter.PNG/600px-Incenter.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption>Triangle <i>ABC</i> with <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">incenter</a> <i>I</i>, with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_bisector\" title=\"Angle bisector\">angle bisectors</a> (red), <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Incircle\" title=\"Incircle\">incircle</a> (blue), and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inradius\" title=\"Inradius\">inradii</a> (green)</figcaption></figure> \n<p>The <b>incenter</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> is the intersection of its (interior) <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_bisector\" title=\"Angle bisector\">angle bisectors</a>.  The incenter is the center of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Incircle\" title=\"Incircle\">incircle</a>.  Every <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nondegenerate\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nondegenerate\">nondegenerate</a> triangle has a unique incenter.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_of_Existence\">Proof of Existence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Incenter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof of Existence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of the respective interior angle bisectors of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angles</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edcdc0d73ef64ec441f60a3a8dccdbd10aa61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a4b93e653d03c2dae64d49e5d2591c9615cbd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBA$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  We observe that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lies on an angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edcdc0d73ef64ec441f60a3a8dccdbd10aa61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, is equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />; likewise, it is equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />; hence it is equidistant from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and therefore lies on an angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21361fc8f29984fa3e95bfc0e578efdbce08c736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  Since it lies within the triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, this is the interior angle bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21361fc8f29984fa3e95bfc0e578efdbce08c736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is equidistant from all three sides of the triangle, it is the incenter. \n</p><p>It should be noted that this proof parallels that for the existence of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a>.\n</p><p>The proofs of existence for the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Excenter\" title=\"Excenter\">excenters</a> is the same, except that certain angle bisectors are exterior.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties_of_the_Incenter\">Properties of the Incenter</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Incenter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Properties of the Incenter\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> The incenter of any triangle lies within the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocentroidal_circle&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Orthocentroidal circle (page does not exist)\">orthocentroidal circle</a>.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> The unnormalised <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Areal_coordinates\" title=\"Areal coordinates\">areal coordinates</a> of the incenter are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d534b942086dae501cbdce030206adb87567bb07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bullet$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcircle\" title=\"Circumcircle\">circumcircle</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/5862947b38a495ec9be80e5b9c7582de6cf0d269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />. Then points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lie on a circle centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/e/bce3bd31dd1a0032109a2941894b6c1df90e8c37.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]defaultpen(fontsize(8)); pair A=(7,10), B=(0,0), C=(10,0), D, I; I=incenter(A,B,C); draw(A--B--C--A);draw(circumcircle(A,B,C));draw(incircle(A,B,C)); D=intersectionpoint(A+0.1*expi((angle(B-A)+angle(C-A))/2)--A+20*expi((angle(B-A)+angle(C-A))/2), circumcircle(A,B,C)); draw(A--D);draw(circumcircle(B,C,I)); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^I);label(&quot;A&quot;,A,(0,1));label(&quot;B&quot;,B,(-1,0));label(&quot;C&quot;,C,(1,0)); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,(0,-1));label(&quot;I&quot;,I,(-1,1));[/asy]\" width=\"465\" height=\"668\" /></center>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018091031\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 145/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5464/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.372      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.372      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2117:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018091031 and revision id 43247. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}